// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row elided_param_regions_invariant_compare_admits (tier 2).
// ILLEGAL PROGRAM ADMITTED: TWO DISTINCT ELIDED PARAMETER REGIONS COMPARE EQUAL UNDER AN INVARIANT POINTEE.
//
// `fn f(x: *mut &i64, y: *mut &i64)` has two different anonymous regions, and a `*mut` is invariant over its pointee,
// so `x == y` has no common type: rustc refuses ("lifetime may not live long enough", the error upstream
// tests/ui/nll/type-check-pointer-comparisons.rs prints at compare_mut with the regions written). Legality
