// TODAY admitted and runs (build c52dcb19dff987ff 43; also base baa2a38e8b650fb3 43). The comparison arm IS reached:
// the NAMED spelling `fn f<'a, 'b>(x: *mut &'a i64, y: *mut &'b i64)` is refused today with "operator '==': lifetime
// may not live long enough — *mut &'a i64 and *mut &'b i64 have no common type". It is the two ELIDED regions that
// read as one: hand r24 (`same<T>(x, y)` over the same parameters) and r25 (a let) admit the same pair on both
// builds, so the plane is elision, not the operator.
// ⚠ spec `region.outlives.permissive-elided-source` ("Elided longer side treated as compatible at coercion sites")
// carries NO divergence marker and speaks of an elided SOURCE against a NAMED target; here both sides are elided
// parameters, and neither registry (docs/DIVERGENCES.md A1..A17, docs/spec/divergences.md) names elision. The same
// question at a different site is the row ptr_coercion_cast_door_elided_let_region_admits.
// Found: hand r22, round 2026-09-14e-thruref — "PREDICTIONS.md predicted r22 refused under cmpinv — wrong: the elided
